long_description:
You pass through a series of nature reserves, you come across several sheepfolds, some abandoned, others functional, so also with guard dogs during the summer and autumn. The route offers you the opportunity to see some of the highlights of the Putna-Vrancea Natural Park:
Coza Strait, a canyon which you enter at water level, and then admire from above;
Cârnituri sheepfold with the adjacent clearing, with a panorama that you can hardly part with in order to move on;
Coza Towers, two prominent rock formations that seem to jut out sideways from the trail just to spite those suffering from vertigo, who can't climb up to the lookout point here;
Cristianu Saddle with superb views on one side and the other of the mountain, towards bucolic plains, rich forests, and snowy peaks at the beginning of spring.
Although the route could stop somewhere at 3/4, on Coza Peak, it continues for more than an hour only to climb Golul Cozei rock, for more beautiful panoramas. The climb on top is not signposted, so few know about it. But once you get there, you have a 360-degree view all around.
